<title>USA: Sonus Q4 shr profit $0.28 vs pro forma loss.</title>
<headline>Sonus Q4 shr profit $0.28 vs pro forma loss.</headline>
<dateline>BOTHELL, Wash. 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>SONUS PHARMACEUTICALS, INC.</p>
<p>			Condensed Statements of Operations</p>
<p>		   (in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>			    Three Months Ended  Twelve Months Ended</p>
<p>					     December 31,  December 31,</p>
<p>					 1996     1995    1996     1995</p>
<p> Revenue			   $5,400     $400 $16,600   $4,500</p>
<p>Operating expenses:</p>
<p>   Research and development   1,801    2,987  11,181    7,190</p>
<p>General and administrative</p>
<p>					1,148	575   3,807    2,226</p>
<p> Total operating expenses     2,949    3,562  14,988    9,416</p>
<p> Operating income (loss)	2,451  (3,162)   1,612  (4,916)</p>
<p> Other income (expense), net    286    (101)     620    (491)</p>
<p>Income (loss) before income</p>
<p>   taxes			    2,737  (3,061)   2,232  (5,407)</p>
<p> Income taxes			  90	 40     510	532</p>
<p> Net income (loss)		2,647  (3,101)   1,722  (5,939)</p>
<p> Net income (loss) per share*  0.28   (0.40)    0.19   (0.99)</p>
<p>Shares used in computing net</p>
<p>  income (loss) per share*    9,322    7,803   8,999    5,981</p>
<p>NOTE: *  Per share amounts for 1995 are on a pro forma basis which gives effect to the conversion of redeemable preferred stock, a subordinated debenture and certain deferred revenue plus related accrued interest.</p>
</text>
